    "title": "Police: Man shot, killed near Schiller Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mark Ludwiczak ,\n2 hours ago\nBUFFALO, N.Y. (WIVB) — A man was shot and killed Wednesday night near Schiller Park, Buffalo Police said.\nOfficers responded to a shooting call near Schiller Park around 8:30 p.m., officials said. Police found a man lying in the street on Sprenger Avenue who was bleeding from the head; he was pronounced dead at the scene.\nPolice said that initial reports are that a fight on the basketball court escalated into a fatal shooting. Homicide detectives are investigating, and anyone with any information is asked to call or text 911 or the Buffalo Police confidential tip line at 716-847-2255.\nLatest Local News 50-year-old facing DWI, Leandra’s Law charges Station 12 timeline reaches major milestone Golisano Institute prepares to build business innovation in Buffalo Shelter in place order lifted in Fredonia Lengthy legal fight over Albert the Alligator finally comes to an end ***\nMark Ludwiczak joined the News 4 team in 2024. He is a veteran journalist with two decades of experience in Buffalo. You can follow him online at @marklud12 .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to News 4 Buffalo.",
    "summary": "Officers responded to a shooting call near Schiller Park around 8:30 p.m., officials said. Police found a man lying in the street on Sprenger Avenue who was bleeding from the head; he was pronounced dead at the scene. Police said that initial reports are that a fight on the basketball court escalated into a fatal shooting. Homicide detectives are investigating, and anyone with any information is asked to call or text 911 or the Buffalo Police confidential tip line at 716-847-2255.",
